From 74dacb89cc09730cc2f0e265a136520d21eea4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T0 <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:29:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T2+T4: transfer and disposal contracts

Error catalogues, DTOs and localization for API 4.10. No logic yet.

Delivered together and ahead of T3 because the repository signatures in T3
reference the list filters, exactly as IStockRepo references StockListFilter.

- TransferErrors: 33 codes covering creation, Known-way card selection and
  settlement. Stock-level failures deliberately reuse StockErrors so a
  transfer surfaces the same code a card status change would.
- DisposalErrors: 13 codes. Strict by design - disposal destroys quantity
  and cannot be undone, so ambiguous requests are refused, not interpreted.
- Transfer DTOs: create, receive (carrying the disposition model), dispose,
  list/detail responses and filter. ProductReceiveOutcome is a DTO-level
  enum per ERD 4.5 - computed at query time, never a column.
- Disposal DTOs: standalone dispose by card ids or by quantity, plus list
  and detail projections.
- 46 localized messages added to Messages.resx and Messages.ar.resx.

Verified: every error code has a key in both resource files, no orphans,
and every {0} placeholder matches a WithArg call.
